        "limitation": "Complexity is only measured on the inputs the agent generates",
        "example": "add_slow_branch.c spins for billions of iterations when the first number exceeds 2,000,000,000. The problem has no size parameter, so the estimator always profiles the sample input '7 5' and reports O(1) with full marks, even though two hidden tests time out.",
        "mitigation": "Use worst-case inputs in the generator and only trust this metric for problems that have a size parameter."
